# The image is built with `COPY . .`, so anything here would otherwise be
# baked into the production image. Two of these mattered in practice:
#
#   .env   — app/config.py calls load_dotenv(override=True), so a baked .env
#            OUTRANKS Railway's own variables. Every `railway up` shipped the
#            developer's local settings to production and silently overrode
#            the configured ones. It also put real secrets in an image layer.
#   .venv  — 167MB of local virtualenv, wrong platform, copied for nothing.
#
# Git-triggered builds never see .env (it is gitignored), but `railway up`
# uploads the working directory as-is, so this file is what actually protects
# the image regardless of how it is built.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
venv/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

tests/
.git/
.gitignore
*.log
.DS_Store
